// Generated by mappings/generate-conceptmaps.py from mappings/BeModelEncounter-to-BeEncounter.csv
// Do not edit by hand - edit the CSV and regenerate.

Instance: BeModelEncounter2BeEncounter
InstanceOf: ConceptMap
Usage: #definition
* url = "https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/core-clinical/ConceptMap/BeModelEncounter2BeEncounter"
* name = "BeModelEncounter2BeEncounter"
* title = "BeModelEncounter to BeEncounter Mapping"
* status = #draft
* experimental = false
* description = "Mapping from BeModelEncounter (Logical Model) to be-encounter"
* sourceUri = "https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/core-clinical/StructureDefinition/BeModelEncounter"
* targetUri = "https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/core-clinical/StructureDefinition/be-encounter"

* group[+]
  * source = "https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/core-clinical/StructureDefinition/BeModelEncounter"
  * target = "https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/core-clinical/StructureDefinition/be-encounter"
  * insert ConceptMapElement(identifier, Unique business identifier of the CareSet, Encounter.identifier, Identifier(s\) by which this encounter is known, equivalent, 1..* MS)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(recordedDate, Date of registration by the Author/Recorder (date of the last update\), Encounter.extension:recordedDate, BeExtRecordedDate (be-core\), equivalent, Neither R4 nor R5 Encounter has a recorded/recordedDate element; carried by the be-core extension be-ext-recorded-date (context DomainResource\)\, constrained to 1..1.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(author, The health professional who takes responsibility for the recorded content, Encounter.extension:recorder, BeExtRecorder (be-core\), equivalent, R4 Encounter has no recorder/author element; carried by the be-core extension be-ext-recorder\, constrained to 1..1.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(status, Registration status\, the moment in the lifecycle, Encounter.status, planned | arrived | triaged | in-progress | onleave | finished | cancelled | entered-in-error, inexact, R4 required binding on Encounter.status is kept. The CareSet's VS_Encounter_Status values (final\, corrected\, completed\) are not R4 codes - 'completed' corresponds to 'finished'.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(class, Classification of the type of Encounter, Encounter.class, Classification of patient encounter, narrower, CareSet says 0..*; R4 Encounter.class is a mandatory single Coding and cannot be relaxed or repeated. classHistory is not used.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(serviceType, Type of services/specialisation offered during the Encounter, Encounter.serviceType, Specific type of service, equivalent, R4 element carries the first/primary service type (0..1\). Binding to VS_Encounter_ServiceType (see VS_Be_ServiceType_Voorstel.xlsx\) still to be defined.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(serviceType, Type of services/specialisation offered during the Encounter - additional occurrences, Encounter.extension:additionalServiceType, BeExtCodeableConcept (be-core\), equivalent, CareSet says 0..*; the repeats are carried by be-ext-codeableconcept. The R5 pre-adoption extension extension-Encounter.serviceType is NOT usable: R5 typed serviceType as CodeableReference\, so that extension only carries the Reference(HealthcareService\) half.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(subject, The person who is the subject of the healthcare the record (CareSet\) refers to, Encounter.subject, The patient present at the encounter, equivalent, only Reference(BePatient\))
  * insert ConceptMapElement(episodeOfCare, Reference to the EpisodeOfCare resource this Encounter is linked to, Encounter.episodeOfCare, Episode(s\) of care that this encounter should be recorded against, equivalent, Targets the base EpisodeOfCare resource - there is no BeEpisodeOfCare in be-core (one exists in patient-dossier\). Marked *TODO* in the profile.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(basedOn, The request that initiated this Encounter (can only originate from a CarePlan\), Encounter.extension:basedOn, BeExtEncounterBasedOn (this IG\), equivalent, R4 Encounter.basedOn only allows Reference(ServiceRequest\)\, so a local extension carrying Reference(CarePlan\) was defined. Targets the base CarePlan resource - BeCarePlan is disabled (.fshNO\) in this IG.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(careTeam, Reference to the CareTeam resource recording which team is involved in the care, Encounter.extension:careTeam, extension-Encounter.careTeam (R5 pre-adoption\), equivalent, R4 Encounter has no careTeam; the R5 cross-version extension is used (hl7.fhir.extensions.r5 is already a dependency\). Targets the base CareTeam resource - there is no BeCareTeam in be-core.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(partOf, Reference to another Encounter this Encounter is part of, Encounter.partOf, Another Encounter this encounter is part of, equivalent, only Reference(BeEncounter\))
  * insert ConceptMapElement(serviceProvider, Organisation responsible for this Encounter, Encounter.serviceProvider, The organization (facility\) responsible for this encounter, equivalent, only Reference(BeOrganization\))
  * insert ConceptMapElement(participant, List of participants involved in the care during this Encounter, Encounter.participant, List of participants involved in the encounter, equivalent, participant.individual only Reference(BePractitioner or BePractitionerRole\))
  * insert ConceptMapElement(participant.period, Period during which the Participant is involved in this Encounter, Encounter.participant.period, Period of time during the encounter that the participant participated, equivalent, constrained to 1..1 per the CareSet)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(participant.role, Role of the Participant involved in this Encounter, Encounter.participant.type, Role of participant in encounter, equivalent, R4 names this element 'type'; constrained to 1..1 per the CareSet.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(actualPeriod, The effective start and end moments of this Encounter, Encounter.period, The start and end time of the encounter, equivalent, R5 renamed R4 Encounter.period to actualPeriod - same element.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(length, Effective duration of the Encounter (excluding absences\), Encounter.length, Quantity of time the encounter lasted (less time absent\), equivalent, )
  * insert ConceptMapElement(reason, The list of Reasons that will be discussed during this Encounter, Encounter.reasonCode, Coded reason the encounter takes place, narrower, R5 Encounter.reason.value (CodeableReference\) is split in R4 into reasonCode and reasonReference; reasonReference is kept MS and restricted to Condition/Procedure/Observation.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(diagnosis, List of diagnoses relevant for this Encounter, Encounter.extension:diagnosis, BeExtCodeableReference (be-core\), equivalent, CodeableReference backport\, so a diagnosis can be given as a code\, as a reference to BeProblem\, or both. extension[diagnosis].extension[reference].value[x] only Reference(BeProblem\).)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(diagnosis, List of diagnoses relevant for this Encounter - native R4 element, Encounter.diagnosis.condition, The diagnosis or procedure relevant to the encounter, equivalent, Kept alongside the extension because Encounter.diagnosis also carries use and rank; only Reference(BeProblem\).)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(admission, Details about the admission of the patient to the care organisation, Encounter.hospitalization, Details about the admission to a healthcare service, equivalent, R5 renamed R4 Encounter.hospitalization to admission.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(admission.origin, The location the patient came from for the admission, Encounter.hospitalization.origin, The location/organization from which the patient came before admission, narrower, R4 allows Reference(Location|Organization\); constrained to BeOrganization per the CareSet.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(admission.admitSource, How the patient was admitted, Encounter.hospitalization.admitSource, From where patient was admitted, equivalent, R4 binding to encounter-admit-source is kept.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(admission.reAdmission, Is this a re-admission of the patient?, Encounter.hospitalization.reAdmission, The type of hospital re-admission that has occurred, inexact, The CareSet phrases this as a yes/no question (boolean in the logical model\); R4 types it as CodeableConcept\, which cannot be changed in a profile.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(admission.destination, Destination of the patient after discharge, Encounter.hospitalization.destination, Location/organization to which the patient is discharged, narrower, R4 allows Reference(Location|Organization\); constrained to BeOrganization per the CareSet.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(admission.dischargeDisposition, Category of location after discharge of the patient, Encounter.hospitalization.dischargeDisposition, Category or kind of location after discharge, equivalent, R4 binding to encounter-discharge-disposition is kept.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(note, Additional information related to the CareSet content in free text form, Encounter.extension:note, BeExtSimpleNote (be-core\), equivalent, R4 Encounter has no note element; carried by the be-core extension be-ext-simple-note.)
